KG42.register("rules-e5b6da36970bb626b7a57c12",{"id":"42-data_center_space_time_flexibility::v141-c-R014","paper":"42-data_center_space_time_flexibility","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R014","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M04","name":"Market payment","process_stage":"settlement","market_meaning":"Each consumer is charged the electricity price at its hub node and remunerated for shifting services; virtual links are paid using the price difference between sending and receiving nodes. Scope: General spatial virtual-link market; consumers and their virtual-link shifting services.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function settlement.payment under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["settlement.payment"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"General spatial virtual-link market; consumers and their virtual-link shifting services.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e031"]},"x":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R014-X001","symbol":"d_j","meaning":"Cleared load allocation (load withdrawn) for consumer j, used as a settlement input.","kind":"operational","domain":"d_j \\in C_d (cleared-load domain in the spatial clearing formulation (2.29e))","unit":null,"indices":["j\\in D"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e030","v141-b-g02-e031"]},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R014-X002","symbol":"\\delta_v","meaning":"Cleared load shift (virtual flow) on virtual link v, used as a settlement input.","kind":"operational","domain":"[0,\\bar\\delta_v]","unit":null,"indices":["v\\in V"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e026","v141-b-g02-e031"]}],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R014-T001","symbol":"\\pi_n","meaning":"Cleared nodal electricity price at node n (dual of nodal balance), used to charge consumers and remunerate virtual links.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"cleared nodal price \\pi_n"},"unit":null,"indices":["n\\in N"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e030","v141-b-g02-e031"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R014-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Each consumer is charged the electricity price at its hub node and remunerated for shifting services; virtual links are paid using the price difference between sending and receiving nodes. Scope: General spatial virtual-link market; consumers and their virtual-link shifting services.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e031"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R014-C002","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"For each consumer j in D, the consumer is charged the electricity price at its hub node for its cleared load d_j, so the consumer charge is charge_j = pi_{n_h(j)} d_j.","expression":"\\text{charge}_j = \\pi_{n_h(j)} d_j,\\quad j\\in D","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R014-X001"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R014-T001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e031","v141-b-g02-e030","v141-b-g02-e026"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R014-C003","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"For each virtual link v in V, the market pays the virtual link by the price difference between its sending and receiving nodes, so the virtual-link payment is payment_v = (pi_{snd(v)} - pi_{rec(v)}) delta_v.","expression":"\\text{payment}_v = (\\pi_{snd(v)} - \\pi_{rec(v)})\\,\\delta_v,\\quad v\\in V","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R014-X002"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R014-T001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e031","v141-b-g02-e026","v141-b-g02-e030"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R014-C004","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"For each consumer j in D, the shifting-service remuneration received through the consumer's virtual links V_j is remuneration_j = sum over v in V_j of (pi_{snd(v)} - pi_{rec(v)}) delta_v.","expression":"\\text{remuneration}_j = \\sum_{v\\in V_j} (\\pi_{snd(v)} - \\pi_{rec(v)})\\,\\delta_v,\\quad j\\in D","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R014-X002"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R014-T001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e031","v141-b-g02-e026","v141-b-g02-e030"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e031","location":{"location_id":"src-1c03246cb9-p08-c1r3__v141-a-M04-pricing","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.5 Basic formulation with general virtual links (spatial)","anchor_text":"(e.g., data transfer costs). In this market, each consumer 𝑗∈is charged with the electricity price ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"where the set C_{\\delta}:=\\{\\delta | \\delta_v\\in[0,\\bar\\delta_v] \\forall v\\in V\\} captures the capacity constraints for virtual links. Comparing this formulation with the previous formulation (2.23), we observe that the social surplus (2.29a) now captures the operational cost of virtual links; moreover, the balance constraints (2.29b) now include spatial virtual shifts. The dual variables associated with the computing capacity constraints (2.29d) are denoted \\omega^{l}_n and \\omega^{u}_n, respectively. Note that the operational cost of virtual links resembles that of operational costs of physical transmission and, as the name suggest, these capture costs associated with load shifting (e.g., data transfer costs). In this market, each consumer j\\in D is charged with the electricity price at the hub node and also remunerated by the shifting service provided through virtual links. As shown in Section 2.4, the market pays off virtual links by the price difference between the sending and receiving nodes."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e026","location":{"location_id":"src-1c03246cb9-p07-c2r3__v141-a-M04-bidding","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.5 Basic formulation with general virtual links (spatial)","anchor_text":"2.5. Basic formulation with general virtual links (spatial) We now generalize the concept of virtual","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"We let V be the set of all virtual links; each virtual link v\\in V has an associated bid price \\alpha^{\\delta}_{v}\\in R_+ and capacity \\bar\\delta_v\\in[0,\\infty). The cleared load shifts (virtual flows) are defined as \\delta_v\\in R_+ and are subject to capacity constraints \\delta_v\\in[0,\\bar\\delta_v]. We define V^{snd}_n:=\\{v\\in V | snd(v)=n\\}\\subseteq V, V^{rec}_n:=\\{v\\in V | rec(v)=n\\}\\subseteq V to be the set of sending and receiving virtual links at node n. Each flexible consumer j\\in D is associated with a set of virtual links V_j\\subseteq V. For each v\\in V_j, snd(v)=n_h(j) since each consumer can only bid flexibility going from its hub node to other alternative nodes."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e030","location":{"location_id":"src-1c03246cb9-p08-c1r2__v141-a-M04-clearing","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.5 Basic formulation with general virtual links (spatial)","anchor_text":"∑ ∑ + 𝑑𝑗+ 𝛿𝑣, (𝜋𝑛) 𝑛∈ (2.29b) m 𝑗∈𝑛 𝑣∈rec𝑛 𝑑, 𝑓𝑙+ −𝑓𝑙−= 𝐵𝑙(𝜃snd(𝑙) −𝜃rec(𝑙)), 𝑙∈ (2.29c) s. ∑ ∑ ","equation_id":"2.29","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The market clearing problem with spatial virtual links is: min_{d,p,f,\\theta,\\delta}\\sum_{i\\in S}\\alpha^{p}_{i}p_i+\\sum_{k\\in K}\\alpha^{f}_{k}f_k+\\sum_{v\\in V}\\alpha^{\\delta}_{v}\\delta_v-\\sum_{j\\in D}\\alpha^{d}_{j}d_j (2.29a) s.t. \\sum_{k\\in K^{rec}_n}f_k+\\sum_{i\\in S_n}p_i+\\sum_{v\\in V^{snd}_n}\\delta_v=\\sum_{k\\in K^{snd}_n}f_k+\\sum_{j\\in D_n}d_j+\\sum_{v\\in V^{rec}_n}\\delta_v, (\\pi_n) n\\in N (2.29b); f_{l^+}-f_{l^-}=B_l(\\theta_{snd(l)}-\\theta_{rec(l)}), l\\in L (2.29c); 0\\le\\sum_{j\\in D_n}d_j+\\sum_{v\\in V^{rec}_n}\\delta_v-\\sum_{v\\in V^{snd}_n}\\delta_v\\le\\bar d^{max}_n, (\\omega^{l}_n,\\omega^{u}_n) n\\in N (2.29d); d\\in C_d, p\\in C_p, \\theta\\in C_\\theta, \\delta\\in C_\\delta (2.29e)."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":null,"empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M04-pricing","v141-a-M04-settlement"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"settlement.payment","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e031","quote":"In this market, each consumer j\\in D is charged with the electricity price at the hub node and also remunerated by the shifting service provided through virtual links. As shown in Section 2.4, the market pays off virtual links by the price difference between the sending and receiving nodes."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"04a734f3960362b586b91809848968032810da1404571dbde12cfd5f7012da70","applicability":"formalized","reason":"Formalized the source-stated settlement components as properties of settlement.payment: consumer charge at the hub-node electricity price (C002), virtual-link payment by the sending-minus-receiving nodal price difference (C003), and the consumer's shifting-service remuneration over its virtual links V_j (C004). C001 is preserved as the original procedural statement. The frozen graph contains only the unary settlement.payment node and no edges, so bindings attach to that node; no graph edge is required for these unary source-stated formulas. B evidence remains unreviewed in this experiment.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R014-X001","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The cleared load d_j is the quantity multiplied by the hub-node price in the source-stated consumer charge relation, a unary property of settlement.payment; no graph edge exists or is needed for this binding."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R014-X002","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The cleared virtual flow delta_v is the quantity multiplied by the sending-minus-receiving price difference in the source-stated virtual-link payment relation, a unary property of settlement.payment; no graph edge exists or is needed for this binding."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R014-T001","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The nodal price pi_n is the price input used to charge consumers at hub nodes and to remunerate virtual links by sending-minus-receiving price differences; it attaches to settlement.payment without a graph edge."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R014-C002","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Formalizes the source-stated consumer charge at the hub-node electricity price as a unary property of settlement.payment; the frozen graph has no applicable edge."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R014-C003","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Formalizes the source-stated virtual-link payment by the sending-minus-receiving nodal price difference as a unary property of settlement.payment; the frozen graph has no applicable edge."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R014-C004","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Formalizes the source-stated consumer remuneration for shifting services provided through its virtual links V_j as a unary property of settlement.payment; the frozen graph has no applicable edge."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
